    "Condition : 1 - The London Borough of Hounslow as the Local Planning Authority hereby certify that the proposed outbuilding (6.3m depth x 6m wide with a maximum height of 2.5m) received on the 12 August 2009, and verified on site on the 23 September 2009, as shown on the  drawings submitted on 12 August 2009 and numbered 2009/M/10  was lawful within the meaning of Sections 191 and 192 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 for the following reason:The development complies with the terms of Schedule 2, Part 1, Class E, Clauses E.1(a) and (d) (ii) of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) Order 1995 (as amended in 2008) because the height of the outbuilding would be no greater than 2.5m and within 2m of the site boundary."
